 of animals with the tissue examined histopathologically, multiplied by 100. Abnormal non-neoplastic changes were not detected in thyroid, parathyroid, thymus, stomach, jejunum, ileum, cecum, colon and pituitary.</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap><table-wrap id="pone-0006493-t003" position="float"><object-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1371/journal.pone.0006493.t003</object-id><label>Table 3</label><caption><title>Incidence of non-neoplastic lesions observed in DNA polymerase &#x003b2; Tg mice.</title></caption><alternatives><graphic id="pone-0006493-t003-3" xlink:href="pone.0006493.t003"/><table frame="hsides" rules="groups"><colgroup span="1"><col align="left" span="1"/><col align="center" span="1"/><col align="center" span="1"/><col align="center" span="1"/></colgroup><thead><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Organ</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Macroscopic Finding</td><td colspan="2" align="left" rowspan="1">Frequency (&#x00025;)<xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="nt103">&#x0002a;</xref></td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Male (n&#x0200a;&#x0003d;&#x0200a;15)</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Female (n&#x0200a;&#x0003d;&#x0200a;21)</td></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Ovary</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Atrophy</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02013;</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">94.4</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Cyst</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02013;</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">60.0</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Thrombus</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02013;</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">5.6</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Vagina</td><t